      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I think private instances should be included included in the population count, because then you know which worlds are truly the most popular regardless of whether people use public instances or not. This is to know which worlds are worth checking out until we get a ranking system for them. \n\nMaybe what you are suggesting should apply to the worlds list in the social tab. It should only show public instances you can join. Right now the list is basically useless, because almost all the worlds in that list are either empty or have only private instances.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2019-02-25T05:13:09.367Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Maybe adjusting the \"Population Count\" in worlds to show just people in public instances. Because I keep trying to go to not-so populated maps because it's easier to start a conversation; and every time I would think a map is populated: it's just populated with private instances. For example: I would see in the overall map selection, Dicey Cafe, has 13 people using it. But when I actually clicked to see the instances: They are empty and it says \"Public: 0. Private: 13\". I personally see no reason to show the private population since people, more or less, join maps because of the population. They would be like \"Hey. Someone is there, I can talk to someone\". And showing private population is, in my opinion, lying to the player. Like if a cake shop said they had 20 cakes at the store, but when you go to the cake store: you find out that the 20 cakes there are pre-orders for other customers. See what I mean? Sorry if i'm a broken record. But I honestly think private population shouldn't be accounted for in the overall population count.",
